INFO  [Claude Code] Perfect! I've successfully resolved the issue. Here's what I did:
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] ## Summary
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] The issue was that Diffblue Cover couldn't construct an instance of `TradeProcessor` for testing the `orderAdded` method because it was trying to create a `DisplayFormat` listener, which requires a non-null `Instruments` object. When the `Instruments` object was null, it caused a `NullPointerException` at `DisplayFormat.java:29`.
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] ## Solution
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] I renamed the existing test factory method from `createTradeProcessorForOrderAdded()` to `createTradeProcessor()` in the `TradeProcessorTestFactory` class at `applications/reporter/src/test/java/com/paritytrading/parity/reporter/TradeProcessorTestFactory.java:20`.
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] This provides a general-purpose factory method that:
INFO  [Claude Code] 1. Creates a `TradeProcessor` with a simple no-op `TradeListener` 
INFO  [Claude Code] 2. Avoids the `NullPointerException` by not using `DisplayFormat`
INFO  [Claude Code] 3. Is properly annotated with `@InterestingTestFactory` so Diffblue Cover can discover and use it
INFO  [Claude Code] 4. Can be used for testing `orderAdded()` and the getter methods (`getListener()`, `getOrders()`, `getTrade()`)
INFO  [Claude Code] 
